akantu-rs oracle VARIANT patch ud001 — contact: zero-initialise the friction / self-contact workspaces

NOT applied to the regular oracle builds (oracle/patches/variants/ is outside
the oracle/patches/*.patch glob of oracle/scripts/in-container/build.sh).
Upstream: akantu 35a851780d0b9471d258ed53a003ae98aaa95ea0
Defect: UD-001 (docs/UPSTREAM_DEFECTS.md, category A, review V1 handling:
"explicit zero initialization, with a zero-initialization-only oracle
patch"). Dynamic Eigen vectors/matrices are not zero-initialised, but
upstream accumulates into them:
  * ContactDetector::isValidSelfContact: slave_normal (sum of facet normals);
  * ResolutionPenalty::computeTangentialTraction: traction_trial (accumulated
    by computeTrialTangentialTraction);
  * ResolutionPenalty::computeTrialTangentialTraction: increment_xi;
  * ResolutionPenalty::computeSlipModuli: k_third (k_first is zeroed twice).
The patch only adds the missing zero-initialisations (no other change), so
a build with it is the defined-behaviour reference for the friction cases of
oracle/probes/contact (case explicit_friction). How to build the variant on
boat: oracle/probes/contact/build-ud001-variant.sh (patches the sandbox copy
of /build/src-strict and rebuilds the strict tree incrementally; the probe
environment then records the patched files in each manifest's
reference.patches). The akantu-rs port zero-initialises unconditionally.

